<title>ITALY: Italy's Florence sees Jan CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Florence sees Jan CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCE, Italy 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Florence said its January consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In December, Florence's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.1 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Florence is one of 11 Italian cities which to have published inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.08 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.1)     2.2  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.7   (0.0)     1.5  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1   (0.3)     2.7  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.5   (0.0)     4.0  (5.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0  (-0.1)     2.3  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		   1.9   (0.0)     2.5  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.7   (0.1)     1.0  (0.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.5   (0.2)    -0.5  (0.5)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     3.8  (3.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  1.7   (0.0)     5.2  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.2)     1.5  (1.3)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
